    {
      "id": "b4",
      "function": "demonstration",
      "scene_type": "rv_cutaway",
      "spoken": "Cooler air is denser. More charge fits into the cylinder, and the tendency to knock goes down. The lecture names both as advantages of direct injection. Small turbocharged engines build on exactly that. That is a double benefit.",
