    {
      "id": "b5",
      "function": "insight",
      "scene_type": "rv_readout",
      "spoken": "The US Department of Energy writes that cooler air allows a higher compression ratio or better spark timing. The agency puts the fuel saving at about one percent. According to the lecture, direct injection already had a market share of about forty percent in twenty thirteen.",
